  "body": "Closes #1152\nClaim: cloud/i1152-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1152-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)\n\n**Problem.** The « Aucun post n'a été trouvé » banner vanished after 3 s even under VoiceOver, with no announcement; « Annuler » / « OK » were plain text buttons.\n\n**Cause.** A 3 s `.task` in `FilteredPostsBanner` (not the shared #864 `ConfirmationAutoDismiss`), no `AccessibilityNotification`, no button style.\n\n**Change.** The status goes through `FilteredPostsModel`: `show(status:)` / `clearStatus()`, armed on `ConfirmationAutoDismiss` (4 s, never under VoiceOver) and announced via `ReaderAccessibility.announce` (injectable `announce`). The view timer is removed. Both buttons use `.buttonStyle(.glass)` + `.controlSize(.small)` (the issue's \"or\": no custom 44 pt frame, so none is claimed or measured; Mac check: Accessibility Inspector). Errors and alerts untouched.\n\n**Tests** (`FilteredPostsStatusTests`, new file): stays under VoiceOver (no wait asked); goes after `ConfirmationAutoDismiss.delay` otherwise; announced once; an old wait cannot clear the status of a new run. Linux cannot build the app, so they were not seen red; CI decides.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```changelog\n| UX | Filtre de posts : le message de résultat reste affiché sous VoiceOver (4 s sinon, au lieu de 3 s) et est annoncé. | #1351 | `Favorites.swift:1054-1063` @ `87fe0d1c` |\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEa2SC36KELdXLSvEA)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEa2SC36KELdXLSvEA",
