   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 1)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES** — head 1b764c6\n\n1. **High**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsModelTests.swift:422` and `:372`. CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:28`), and `--strict` turns warnings into errors. The file grows from 359 to 422 lines, which breaks `file_length` (limit 400), and `emptyRun` returns a 3-tuple, which breaks `large_tuple`. The lint job will fail as is. Fix: move `FilteredPostsStatusTests` into its own file (`FilteredPostsStatusTests.swift`), and return a small struct, or keep `Spoken` on the suite, so the function returns no 3-tuple.\n2. **Medium**, `FilteredPostsModelTests.swift` (`aNewRunCancelsThePendingTimer`). This test stays green without the change it is named after (L01). I removed `statusTimer.cancel()` from `clearStatus()` and traced the test: the second `arm()` already bumps the generation, so `finish(0)` is a no-op either way, and `statusMessage == nil` after `start` held before the PR too. Fix: write a scenario where only the cancel helps (start a new run, let its wait end before the run delivers, check nothing changes), or rename the test to what it really checks (an old wait cannot clear a newer status).\n3. **Medium**, `App/SwiftHFR/FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsView.swift:54-61`. The 44 pt hit region is claimed but not measured. `.frame(minHeight: 44).contentShape(.rect)` sits outside the `Button`, and nothing shows the button's own tap region grows with it. The frame also makes the whole banner taller (44 + 16 pt padding), during the progress line too. #1155 and #1156 measured this with a hosted test (`PagerPillTouchTargetTests`). Fix: add the same measurement for `bannerButton()` (width and height ≥ 44 at `.xSmall` and `.large`), or rely on the bordered glass style alone (the issue accepts \"or\") and drop the 44 pt claim.\n4. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFR/Common/ConfirmationAutoDismiss.swift:4-8`. The doc comment still says the timer is for HFR success confirmations only. It now also clears an informational status, and that status's delay changes from legacy's 3 s to 4 s. Fix: update the doc comment (L08) and state the 3 s to 4 s difference in the PR's `### Ledger` / gap entry.\n5. **Detail**, `FilteredPostsView.swift:89`. The comment says \"legacy used a 3 s view task\". The view task was the earlier Swift port; legacy hid the line after 3 s. Fix: correct the wording.\n\n**Verified**: I read the diff, `ConfirmationAutoDismiss`, `ManualSleeper`, `ReaderAccessibility.announce` and the whole of `FilteredPostsModel`, and found no Swift 6 isolation problems (everything is `@MainActor`; `[weak self]` in `arm`). I ran swiftlint on the touched folders: it gives the 2 warnings of finding 1. I did a mental mutation test of `clearStatus` (finding 2). I could not run any app tests: the app does not build on Linux.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
