   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 2)**\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES** — head 06f6790\n\n1. **Medium** (PR body, `### Ledger`). The `changelog` block is a sentence, not a table row. `ledger.py check-body` rejects it with `changelog block 1: one or more rows | T | résumé | lot / PR | preuve | and nothing else`, and the **Docs consistency** check fails on 06f6790 for the same reason. As long as it fails, the PR is not mergeable and the steward would skip it. The row also says the glass buttons are a change from legacy, but legacy already had them (`Favorites.swift:1215-1255`). Fix: write one 4-cell row, for example `| UX | Filtre de posts : le message de résultat reste affiché sous VoiceOver (4 s sinon, au lieu de 3 s) et est annoncé. | #1351 | `Favorites.swift:1054-1063` @ `87fe0d1c` |`. Then run `check-body` locally before pushing.\n2. **Low** (`FilteredPostsView.swift:5-11`). The `// Port of … Differences:` header (AGENTS §4) does not list the new difference from legacy: no timer under VoiceOver, 4 s instead of 3 s, the result is announced. Fix: add one clause.\n3. **Detail** (`FilteredPostsModel.swift:69`). `announce` is a test seam that the `@Observable` macro tracks. Fix: mark it `@ObservationIgnored`.\n\nThe model changes are correct. `start`, `closeResult` and the OK button all go through `clearStatus()`. The shared timer's generation counter stops an old wait from clearing a newer status. `[weak self]` avoids a retain cycle. These mutations would turn the tests red: dropping `announce` (`theStatusIsAnnouncedOnce`) and dropping `arm` (`withoutVoiceOver…`). `underVoiceOver…` only covers the shared timer's VoiceOver check. Covering the issue's \"or\" with glass + small is fine. The Accessibility Inspector hand check still has to be listed on #893.\n\n**Verified**\n- Detached worktree at 06f6790.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` on the touched files: 0 issues.\n- `ledger.py check-body` on the current PR body: error above.\n- Check runs on 06f6790: Docs consistency fails; App build is skipped by the draft gate.\n- Legacy citations checked at `87fe0d1c` (`Favorites.swift:1054-1063`, 3 s timer).\n- The issue's acceptance criteria are each covered.\n- App tests were not run: the app does not build on Linux.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
