   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 3)**\n\n**APPROVE** — head d4cb5ba\n\nChecked against #1152:\n- **Timer:** the banner's 3 s view `.task` is gone. The status now goes through `ConfirmationAutoDismiss`, which waits 4 s and is never armed under VoiceOver. `start`, `closeResult` and `dismissStatus` all go through `clearStatus()`, so the timer is cancelled with them. The timer's generation guard stops an old wait from clearing a newer status (the `anOldWaitCannotClearTheStatusOfANewRun` test covers this).\n- **Announcement:** the status is announced once when it is set. `ReaderAccessibility.announce` is `@MainActor (String?)`, so the `@MainActor (String) -> Void` default closure type-checks.\n- **Buttons:** both use `.buttonStyle(.glass)` with `.controlSize(.small)`. That is the issue's first option (\"bordered style\"), and the PR body says no 44 pt frame is claimed.\n- **Compiler rigour (read, not built):** `@ObservationIgnored var` with a closure default in a `@MainActor @Observable` class is fine. `let statusTimer` is not tracked, the same as `confirmationTimer` in `TopicReaderModel`. The test helpers exist with matching signatures: `ManualSleeper.sleep` as `@MainActor (Duration) async throws`, `FakeFilteredSource(handler:)`, `filteredBatch(posts:)`, `filterTopic` and `settle()`. The non-Sendable `Spoken` is only captured by a `@MainActor` closure in a `@MainActor` suite.\n\nFindings:\n1. **Detail.** `FilteredPostsView.swift` (`bannerButton`): the doc comment says \"capsule\", but `.buttonBorderShape(.capsule)` is not set, unlike legacy `Favorites.swift:1215-1255`. The glass style's automatic shape should already be a capsule. Fix: add `.buttonBorderShape(.capsule)`, or drop the word from the comment.\n2. **Detail.** `FilteredPostsView.swift`, banner `.accessibilityElement(children: .combine)`: under VoiceOver, « OK » is now the only way to remove the line, inside a combined element. Fix: add a VoiceOver activation of « OK » to the device check of #893.\n3. **Detail.** Commit 1b764c6's title still says \"44 pt hit region\". The PR body is right; the squash message should say \"bordered glass buttons\".\n\n**Checked:** read the diff, the full `FilteredPostsModel`, `ConfirmationAutoDismiss`, `ReaderAccessibility`, the test helpers in `ConfirmationAutoDismissTests.swift` and `FilteredPostsModelTests.swift`, and the issue body over REST. Ran `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 4 touched files: 0 violations. Not built or run, because Linux cannot build the app; CI decides on the tests.\n\nThe three details are left as is so the APPROVE stays on d4cb5ba: finding 1 is a comment wording, 2 goes on the #893 device check, 3 is for whoever squash-merges (message: \"bordered glass buttons\").\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
